<div id="collection" class="project-stage-heading case-study-anchor"><span>05</span><div><small>AUTOMATED DATA COLLECTION</small><h3>One collection platform for both calibration systems</h3></div></div>

<p>I designed and implemented a shared <strong>Airflow / Kubernetes</strong> collection platform for camera–LiDAR and LiDAR–LiDAR learning, then worked with infrastructure and operations teams to review and launch it in <strong>two regions</strong>. A single streaming read of each drive log produces both datasets, with one independently retryable Pod per log.</p>

<p>The October collection streamed <strong>17+ TB of raw drive logs</strong> through single-pass extraction, producing <strong>~600 GB of camera–LiDAR and LiDAR–LiDAR calibration data</strong>. These are shared collection totals for both models; curated training-set sizes are reported separately for each model.</p>

